WEBVTT

00:00:03.370 --> 00:00:07.370
I still feel terrible for what I did,
but let's not dwell on that.

00:00:07.570 --> 00:00:10.770
Well, it's not as if I'm the only
one that embarrassed herself.

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:14.110
We tried to forget about the
war for a short while,

00:00:14.110 --> 00:00:15.940
but Enemy-san is just so intense.

00:00:16.210 --> 00:00:19.050
I wonder if we've all become adults
who only know how to fight?

00:00:38.350 --> 00:00:43.310
Kuyashisa wo koraete keri ageta ishikoro

00:00:38.350 --> 00:00:43.310
Bearing your grief, you kick a stone.

00:00:45.310 --> 00:00:50.320
Hane kaereba DAIMOND ni mo naru

00:00:45.310 --> 00:00:50.320
It might turn into a diamond when it bounces back.

00:00:52.150 --> 00:00:56.950
Sugu te ni hairu yume nante yume janaiyo

00:00:52.150 --> 00:00:56.950
The dream that comes true so easily isn't really a dream.

00:00:58.910 --> 00:01:03.830
Demo kanarazu kanau to shinjiteru yo

00:00:58.910 --> 00:01:03.830
Still, you believe that it will become real.

00:01:05.630 --> 00:01:12.220
Kujikenai kimi ga suki...

00:01:05.630 --> 00:01:12.220
I like you, because you never give in.

00:01:12.220 --> 00:01:15.640
Nakitai toki aru nara

00:01:12.220 --> 00:01:15.640
When you want to cry,

00:01:15.640 --> 00:01:19.600
soba ni zutto zutto iru kara

00:01:15.640 --> 00:01:19.600
I'll be with you.

00:01:20.010 --> 00:01:21.680
YOU GET TO BURNING

00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:26.900
Kimi rashiku hoko rashiku mukatte yo

00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:26.900
Fight honourably, as you should.

00:01:26.900 --> 00:01:32.690
Muchuu ni natta hibi ga yume no kakera sa

00:01:26.900 --> 00:01:32.690
The days when you can devote yourself are the pieces of your dream.

00:01:33.530 --> 00:01:35.360
YOU GET TO BURNING

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:38.410
Sono kakera wo atsumete

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:38.410
Gathering those pieces,

00:01:38.410 --> 00:01:40.280
asu wo mezasu

00:01:38.410 --> 00:01:40.280
you can show your courage

00:01:40.280 --> 00:01:43.120
yuuki, mieru yo

00:01:40.280 --> 00:01:43.120
to aim for tomorrow.

00:01:43.120 --> 00:01:50.040
To be... Going your day's. Grow up!

00:02:06.850 --> 00:02:08.310
You get to burning.

00:02:08.380 --> 00:02:13.290
Go forward being yourself, being proud.

00:02:13.290 --> 00:02:15.790
The days you spent wrapped up in a dream...

00:02:15.790 --> 00:02:18.760
...are a piece of your drapes.

00:02:18.860 --> 00:02:19.480
Oops.

00:02:20.060 --> 00:02:21.080
Dreams!

00:02:21.330 --> 00:02:23.660
Captain, I won't have you
singing moronic songs!

00:02:24.430 --> 00:02:26.070
We are currently involved in an operation!

00:02:26.070 --> 00:02:30.400
We might be here as the rear guard,
but it's like we were left out in the cold.

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:32.700
I don't blame them, with a crew like this.

00:02:32.940 --> 00:02:34.100
But listen, everyone!

00:02:34.340 --> 00:02:37.430
Our time for slacking off
won't last much longer!

00:02:37.880 --> 00:02:41.440
The tide of war will soon change drastically!

00:02:42.010 --> 00:02:45.550
We will rid the Earth of the Jovian
Lizards and their Chulips!

00:02:45.550 --> 00:02:49.790
And next, we'll invade Mars,
where the Nadesico will...

00:02:47.550 --> 00:02:49.790
Abnormal increase in boson particle readings...

00:02:49.790 --> 00:02:50.980
...from rear hangar.

00:02:57.730 --> 00:02:59.060
This just in from the front.

00:02:59.060 --> 00:03:02.000
One large enemy battleship that
just emerged from the Chulip...

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:03.970
...is now heading directly toward the Nadesico.

00:03:04.300 --> 00:03:07.360
Boson reaction increase now
originating in tip of the Y Unit.

00:03:08.770 --> 00:03:10.540
We have the hostile in our sensors' scopes.

00:03:10.780 --> 00:03:12.300
What's the extent of the damage?

00:03:12.780 --> 00:03:16.270
Rear hangar and Y Unit block three
have been devastated.

00:03:16.820 --> 00:03:18.180
But this is strange.

00:03:18.320 --> 00:03:19.920
There is remarkably little damage, considering...

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:21.350
What the hell's going on?

00:03:21.550 --> 00:03:23.420
What were all those explosions?

00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:27.350
If it wasn't for the distortion blocks,
we would all be dead.

00:03:27.660 --> 00:03:29.030
Distortion blocks?

00:03:29.300 --> 00:03:30.850
Thank you for asking!

00:03:31.700 --> 00:03:33.530
I thought this might happen,

00:03:33.530 --> 00:03:36.640
so I designed a system where
distortion fields compartmentalize...

00:03:36.640 --> 00:03:38.570
all blast damage occurring inside the ship.

00:03:39.940 --> 00:03:45.140
I thought this might happen, so...

00:03:46.110 --> 00:03:48.080
I've been wanting to say
this line for so long!

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:51.780
Hey! You're supposed to be hard
at work repairing the Y unit!

00:03:53.750 --> 00:03:55.880
Ruri-kun, status of enemy vessel.

00:03:56.360 --> 00:03:59.050
Distance, 42 kilometers.
Coming into visual range soon.

00:04:05.830 --> 00:04:07.420
What will you do, Captain?

00:04:07.900 --> 00:04:08.760
Let's run for it.

00:04:10.340 --> 00:04:13.070
Minato-san, all ahead full at
maximum elevation, please.

00:04:13.240 --> 00:04:16.110
No problem, but we'll shoot
up into space if we do that.

00:04:16.110 --> 00:04:17.010
That's just fine.

00:04:17.340 --> 00:04:18.140
Okay.

00:04:18.440 --> 00:04:20.340
Boson reaction increasing again.

00:04:20.510 --> 00:04:22.410
This time, just below the bridge.

00:04:23.250 --> 00:04:24.340
Engines full!

00:04:25.720 --> 00:04:27.310
Nadesico, maximum ascent!

00:04:48.540 --> 00:04:51.010
Enemy ship is increasing speed
and following close behind.

00:04:53.210 --> 00:04:54.800
Persistent jerk!

00:04:55.050 --> 00:04:58.020
Why are we running?!
Let's turn about and hit him back!

00:04:58.180 --> 00:05:01.310
And we'd go ka-boom,
thanks to their new weapon.

00:05:01.520 --> 00:05:03.520
Ryouko wants to be in the midst of
a touchy-feely love explosion...

00:05:03.520 --> 00:05:04.990
Ka-boom!

00:05:05.120 --> 00:05:06.660
Thank you very much.

00:05:06.660 --> 00:05:08.220
Come back here, you damn jerks!

00:05:08.360 --> 00:05:10.190
I said come back here, can't you hear me?!

00:05:11.030 --> 00:05:14.170
Inez-san, have you been able to
determine the explosion's source?

00:05:14.170 --> 00:05:15.600
I'll be right there, so don't go anywhere!

00:05:15.600 --> 00:05:17.660
I'll explain it to you clearly,
concisely, and compassionately!

00:05:19.970 --> 00:05:23.870
I found fragments of explosives in
the gutted blocks that were hit.

00:05:24.180 --> 00:05:26.710
The substance was nearly identical
to the warhead explosives...

00:05:26.710 --> 00:05:28.350
used inside Jovian projectile shells,

00:05:28.350 --> 00:05:31.180
so it's probably safe to assume
they are one and the same.

00:05:31.620 --> 00:05:34.850
It was a bomb? Then it wasn't
an attack from outside?

00:05:34.850 --> 00:05:37.990
All of you here probably
remember the large robots that...

00:05:37.990 --> 00:05:40.360
...the Jovian forces have started deploying.

00:05:40.360 --> 00:05:41.880
Now observe closely!

00:05:42.800 --> 00:05:46.400
Equipped with an on board phase transition
engine, each robot is a formidable weapon...

00:05:46.400 --> 00:05:49.230
...in and of itself, but that is not the reason
why it poses such a terrible threat!

00:05:50.370 --> 00:05:55.400
The most threatening part is that it can execute
boson jumping without the aid of a Chulip.

00:05:55.710 --> 00:06:00.340
So if a robot can teleport
without the aid of a Chulip...

00:06:00.510 --> 00:06:03.810
They should also be able to send out
explosives, missiles, whatever.

00:06:04.280 --> 00:06:04.940
Exactly!

00:06:05.280 --> 00:06:08.720
The abnormal influx of boson
particles prior to the explosion...

00:06:08.720 --> 00:06:12.190
...is probably the same as with the
increases in boson particles...

00:06:12.190 --> 00:06:15.630
...observed when the enemy's Chulip
or robots conduct a boson jump.

00:06:16.530 --> 00:06:20.960
In other words, the enemy was teleporting
explosives directly inside the Nadesico.

00:06:21.170 --> 00:06:23.030
Then, the distortion field...

00:06:23.270 --> 00:06:24.600
Won't be able to defend against it.

00:06:24.900 --> 00:06:27.390
There are practically no effective
defense measures against this.

00:06:27.870 --> 00:06:30.410
I don't know what the accuracy
of their gunnery is,

00:06:30.410 --> 00:06:32.850
but if the bridge or the engine room
were to suffer a direct hit,

00:06:32.850 --> 00:06:34.780
then we'd probably be finished.

00:06:36.150 --> 00:06:37.380
Boson cannon...

00:06:38.120 --> 00:06:39.220
Boson cannon?

00:06:39.220 --> 00:06:42.920
Oh, I just thought this needs a name of its own!

00:06:44.160 --> 00:06:47.130
My boss is really into photography.
Boss owns Canon.

00:06:49.900 --> 00:06:52.090
It's just like Earthlings to run away so easily!

00:06:52.200 --> 00:06:53.530
They don't have any balls.

00:06:53.870 --> 00:06:56.130
It appears they have become
scared of our leap cannon.

00:06:56.340 --> 00:06:57.360
You underestimate them.

00:06:57.570 --> 00:07:01.510
The captain's quick thinking prevented us from
hitting them with the leap cannon's third shot.

00:07:01.870 --> 00:07:03.970
That captain's abilities deserve our respect.

00:07:04.110 --> 00:07:05.600
Aren't you giving them too much credit?

00:07:06.250 --> 00:07:08.080
Even still, remember the old saying.

00:07:08.080 --> 00:07:10.740
When hunting a rabbit, a lion
must enter a tiger's den!

00:07:11.150 --> 00:07:13.390
Make sure to have the Denjin
prepared for launch just in case!

00:07:13.390 --> 00:07:13.940
Aye, aye.

00:07:14.690 --> 00:07:16.020
No way out?

00:07:16.360 --> 00:07:18.190
No, there is a way out.

00:07:18.660 --> 00:07:21.290
If the enemy could, they would have
blown us apart by this time.

00:07:21.660 --> 00:07:24.130
The boson cannon still has shortcomings.

00:07:24.130 --> 00:07:25.460
I see, its range!

00:07:25.460 --> 00:07:26.290
Correct!

00:07:26.600 --> 00:07:29.740
Since the enemy attacked while
it was approaching us,

00:07:29.740 --> 00:07:32.440
the boson cannon must not be
able to strike at long range.

00:07:32.440 --> 00:07:33.340
I see.

00:07:33.570 --> 00:07:37.080
Considering the range at which the enemy
fired the first and second rounds...

00:07:37.080 --> 00:07:40.410
...into the Nadesico, their range is
less than one hundred kilometers!

00:07:40.910 --> 00:07:42.900
Should we go after them in the Aesti?

00:07:43.050 --> 00:07:46.180
Well, chances are we'd get blown
apart before we got close.

00:07:46.620 --> 00:07:51.350
Since they also have a distortion field,
the gravity blast cannon isn't the answer.

00:07:51.890 --> 00:07:53.450
There IS no way out.

00:07:53.530 --> 00:07:55.030
The hell you say, longhair!

00:07:55.030 --> 00:07:56.830
Okay, everyone. Let's be quiet now.

00:07:56.830 --> 00:07:58.730
We have the situation relatively
well-assessed now.

00:07:58.730 --> 00:08:01.790
So, let's listen to what the Captain has to say.

00:08:09.310 --> 00:08:12.210
Are you by chance planning
to suddenly start snoring,

00:08:12.210 --> 00:08:14.440
and do a joke about falling asleep?

00:08:16.420 --> 00:08:17.350
Well?

00:08:19.180 --> 00:08:20.480
Misumaru Yurika?

00:08:21.990 --> 00:08:25.080
Don't be ridiculous. How could
I ever think something like that?

00:08:25.990 --> 00:08:27.650
She was thinking about it.

00:08:27.730 --> 00:08:30.060
Well, why don't we have a
short break for a while.

00:08:30.060 --> 00:08:32.190
Please make a suggestion if you
think of something useful.

00:08:34.600 --> 00:08:36.100
Why are you sighing like that?

00:08:36.100 --> 00:08:37.930
It's not as if we've lost yet.

00:08:38.270 --> 00:08:39.700
No, it's not about that.

00:08:39.770 --> 00:08:42.840
We were out in the ocean, so
Houmei-san was going to teach me...

00:08:42.840 --> 00:08:44.930
...how to fish after the fighting was over.

00:08:45.180 --> 00:08:48.840
That's too bad. This is still a sea,
but it's the sea of stars.

00:08:49.350 --> 00:08:51.610
There are no fish on Mars,

00:08:52.080 --> 00:08:54.420
so I was looking forward to fishing.

00:08:54.650 --> 00:08:55.520
Fishing?

00:08:55.590 --> 00:08:58.250
Akito! What did you just say, Akito?!

00:08:58.560 --> 00:09:01.390
That's it. That's it!
Why didn't I think of it before?!

00:09:01.390 --> 00:09:04.360
Great job, Akito!
Can you repeat what you just said?

00:09:04.930 --> 00:09:06.130
About Houmei-san and I?

00:09:06.130 --> 00:09:07.860
No, not that part.

00:09:08.030 --> 00:09:09.230
F-Fishing?

00:09:09.300 --> 00:09:10.730
Yeah! That's just it!

00:09:10.870 --> 00:09:11.840
Fishing!

00:09:23.480 --> 00:09:24.450
Hurry!

00:09:24.450 --> 00:09:26.790
Reconfigure all the Aestivalis
into their zero gravity frames!

00:09:26.790 --> 00:09:29.810
Chief, are we going to set all the
missiles to timed detonation?

00:09:29.960 --> 00:09:32.620
The Captain said to do it.
The princess' orders!

00:09:32.720 --> 00:09:33.920
Yes, but...

00:09:34.090 --> 00:09:35.750
Just do as you're told and finish it!

00:09:35.860 --> 00:09:36.730
O-Okay!

00:09:36.930 --> 00:09:38.230
What's with the spears?

00:09:38.330 --> 00:09:39.820
Another one of Seiya-san's toys.

00:09:40.070 --> 00:09:43.000
He says that it can neutralize
a field for an instant.

00:09:43.500 --> 00:09:44.900
So, I can do a Passion Slash?

00:09:45.300 --> 00:09:46.200
You fool.

00:09:48.870 --> 00:09:50.710
Come on, get it all to them!

00:09:50.910 --> 00:09:52.980
It's their important meal
before they go on the move.

00:09:52.980 --> 00:09:54.950
We have to make sure they eat right.

00:09:54.950 --> 00:09:56.520
None of them deserve to have to eat C rations.

00:09:56.520 --> 00:09:57.540
Okay!

00:09:57.680 --> 00:09:59.890
Hurry, we have get these bentous
out to the catapult deck...

00:09:59.890 --> 00:10:01.280
...before all the pilots take off.

00:10:01.450 --> 00:10:02.920
Oh, I'll go.

00:10:03.260 --> 00:10:04.980
I want to go too.

00:10:05.290 --> 00:10:07.350
I want to take the one for Akatsuki-san!

00:10:07.760 --> 00:10:09.120
I'll take the one for Akito-san!

00:10:09.360 --> 00:10:11.390
I... Isn't that not such a good idea?

00:10:11.530 --> 00:10:14.290
No problem! I'm not going to take
a back seat to the Captain!

00:10:14.430 --> 00:10:16.960
I... I'd like the one for Ryouko-oneesama.

00:10:18.970 --> 00:10:21.670
This might be the last meal.

00:10:22.510 --> 00:10:25.100
Aestivalis units are all ready to go.

00:10:25.310 --> 00:10:29.580
All missiles have been reset.
Ready to be fired any moment!

00:10:29.680 --> 00:10:32.710
I've turned off all the fires in the galley.
Is that fine, then?

00:10:32.880 --> 00:10:36.820
All unnecessary power consumption
on the ship has been deactivated.

00:10:37.220 --> 00:10:39.750
Preparations for the operation
are all complete. Standing by.

00:10:40.060 --> 00:10:42.580
Then, please shut down the
phase transition engine.

00:10:42.760 --> 00:10:44.560
Engines, shutting down.

00:10:49.270 --> 00:10:52.460
With the engine shut down,
the enemy won't be able to track us.

00:10:52.900 --> 00:10:55.170
But if worse comes to worse,
we will be vulnerable to attack...

00:10:55.170 --> 00:10:56.660
...without the field protecting us.

00:10:57.140 --> 00:10:58.800
Do you think we can win?

00:10:59.210 --> 00:11:00.200
I have faith in them.

00:11:01.280 --> 00:11:03.040
We are up against human beings, right?

00:11:03.620 --> 00:11:04.780
I'm going to put my faith in them.

00:11:14.160 --> 00:11:15.850
Our sensors have lost track
of the enemy vessel!

00:11:15.990 --> 00:11:16.650
What?

00:11:16.800 --> 00:11:21.390
The ship has disappeared off the electronic,
infrared, gravitron wave, and other sensors!

00:11:21.970 --> 00:11:24.800
Going as far as to shutting down all active
sensors, to lurk in silence for us to come.

00:11:24.800 --> 00:11:26.030
Impressive.

00:11:26.340 --> 00:11:29.010
But that means they are practically naked...

00:11:29.010 --> 00:11:31.000
...with their space-time contortion
buffer lowered. Why?

00:11:31.240 --> 00:11:33.980
No defense is effective against the leap cannon!

00:11:33.980 --> 00:11:35.780
We are in far more danger than he is.

00:11:35.780 --> 00:11:36.410
What?

00:11:36.720 --> 00:11:39.380
With all our systems running,
we broadcast all sorts of signals,

00:11:39.380 --> 00:11:41.780
making us clearly visible to passive sensors.

00:11:42.850 --> 00:11:45.020
We'll be in a whole lot of trouble
unless we watch ourselves.

00:11:45.360 --> 00:11:47.660
Cease any further acceleration!
We will observe the situation for a while.

00:11:48.460 --> 00:11:50.000
The enemy has ceased all acceleration.

00:11:50.000 --> 00:11:52.060
Moving at a rate roughly equal to that of ours.

00:11:53.630 --> 00:11:55.470
I fully expected them to
close in without hesitation.

00:11:55.470 --> 00:11:57.490
Seems that they are playing it safe as well.

00:11:57.740 --> 00:11:59.200
Ejecting starboard ballast.

00:11:59.200 --> 00:12:02.330
Changing heading five degrees to port.
Pitch minus two degrees.

00:12:02.870 --> 00:12:04.810
All systems responding normally.

00:12:05.040 --> 00:12:07.640
Captain, it's dangerous to go
without using your seatbelt.

00:12:08.010 --> 00:12:11.570
Well, please say those things... ahead of time!

00:12:11.750 --> 00:12:13.750
I'm impressed at your idea of
using the pressurized air,

00:12:13.750 --> 00:12:16.050
normally used as underwater ballast,
for space maneuvering.

00:12:18.320 --> 00:12:21.120
It looks like all the Aestivalis
units are ready to launch.

00:12:21.190 --> 00:12:23.490
Please have them deployed immediately!

00:12:23.660 --> 00:12:26.260
Manual launching. You got that?

00:12:26.330 --> 00:12:27.160
Roger.

00:12:28.870 --> 00:12:30.900
I just don't like doing this.

00:12:30.900 --> 00:12:32.700
Hey, put in some more feeling, damn it!

00:12:32.700 --> 00:12:33.500
Aye!

00:12:35.170 --> 00:12:36.680
This is so dorky.

00:12:36.680 --> 00:12:38.400
Hey! Keep your distance!

00:12:39.610 --> 00:12:42.440
My, what a peculiar way to take off.

00:12:42.550 --> 00:12:43.880
It's your turn now!

00:12:44.080 --> 00:12:44.950
Okay, okay...

00:12:51.320 --> 00:12:52.760
Good luck, Akito.

00:12:53.160 --> 00:12:55.320
Hey, are you sure about this?

00:12:55.830 --> 00:12:58.730
Floating around this way will
be silly if they shoot at us.

00:12:58.730 --> 00:13:00.130
Yes, don't worry!

00:13:00.500 --> 00:13:02.800
Those people are human beings just like us.

00:13:03.240 --> 00:13:04.460
This will work out!

00:13:04.600 --> 00:13:05.470
Right, right...

00:13:05.800 --> 00:13:07.500
"Akito, Akito," right?

00:13:09.980 --> 00:13:11.700
Prepare gravity wave cannon!

00:13:20.020 --> 00:13:22.890
Enemy gravity blast passing by above.

00:13:23.420 --> 00:13:24.620
Scary...

00:13:25.190 --> 00:13:28.160
No responses coming back from the
path of the gravity wave cannon.

00:13:28.730 --> 00:13:30.720
I suppose they were smart enough
to at least change heading.

00:13:30.960 --> 00:13:32.260
Just can't figure them out.

00:13:32.600 --> 00:13:35.620
They don't have enough firepower for
a surprise attack, so then what?

00:13:38.770 --> 00:13:40.900
Feels strange to just wait here.

00:13:43.580 --> 00:13:45.200
Thou desperate pilot, now at once...

00:13:45.440 --> 00:13:47.100
Free float in space...

00:13:47.480 --> 00:13:49.570
Less filling diet cola float...

00:13:50.050 --> 00:13:52.240
No change in the enemy vessel's
heading and speed.

00:13:52.820 --> 00:13:55.450
Release all missiles in the direction
of the enemy's path.

00:14:01.460 --> 00:14:04.490
Captain, you didn't have to
launch all our missiles.

00:14:04.800 --> 00:14:08.660
After all, missiles are not
cheap pieces of equipment.

00:14:09.070 --> 00:14:13.200
You need to scatter a lot of bait
if you want to catch a big one.

00:14:13.270 --> 00:14:14.330
Oh, please!

00:14:14.770 --> 00:14:16.870
We're up against humans, not fish!

00:14:16.980 --> 00:14:19.210
Yes, they are humans, aren't they?

00:14:19.540 --> 00:14:22.410
That's why they can be counted on
to think and react accordingly.

00:14:23.250 --> 00:14:25.880
Okay, it's about time for us to
return to our original course.

00:14:26.220 --> 00:14:27.120
Minato-san.

00:14:27.620 --> 00:14:28.320
Yes?

00:14:28.320 --> 00:14:29.810
Please change our heading.

00:14:29.960 --> 00:14:30.850
Aye, aye.

00:14:43.800 --> 00:14:45.860
Enemy vessel has come in
contact with missile field.

00:14:46.500 --> 00:14:48.530
It's time to detonate all the missiles, right?

00:14:48.740 --> 00:14:49.430
Not yet!

00:14:49.540 --> 00:14:52.070
Why? Isn't this your strategy?

00:14:52.710 --> 00:14:55.700
If we fire a gravity blast now,
all the missiles will detonate.

00:14:55.980 --> 00:14:56.810
It's pointless.

00:14:57.050 --> 00:14:59.520
It will all be repelled off their distortion field.

00:15:00.050 --> 00:15:01.450
What's your plan, Captain?

00:15:01.890 --> 00:15:03.620
Fishing is all about patience.

00:15:05.990 --> 00:15:07.750
Damn Earthlings, how dare they mock us!

00:15:08.090 --> 00:15:09.320
Where is the point of origin
of these missiles?!

00:15:09.560 --> 00:15:11.190
No single point of origin
can be established, sir!

00:15:11.800 --> 00:15:12.660
Calm down.

00:15:13.470 --> 00:15:15.700
This vessel can withstand
punishment like this with ease!

00:15:15.700 --> 00:15:18.460
Estimate enemy position from the
dispersion pattern of the missiles!

00:15:20.840 --> 00:15:22.470
Probable position of the enemy calculated!

00:15:22.740 --> 00:15:24.830
Right! Change heading to estimated position!

00:15:24.910 --> 00:15:25.570
Wait!

00:15:26.310 --> 00:15:28.510
This is a trap. Do not change heading.

00:15:28.850 --> 00:15:30.140
I am well aware of the trap!

00:15:30.380 --> 00:15:32.520
They may be waiting for us with a
screen of missiles shielding them,

00:15:32.520 --> 00:15:34.180
but we know their position now.

00:15:34.550 --> 00:15:36.820
Do you expect him to be in
the same position still?

00:15:37.160 --> 00:15:38.820
If we go chasing after him now,

00:15:38.820 --> 00:15:41.690
we would jump straight into the
enemy's swarm of missiles.

00:15:41.990 --> 00:15:44.260
Should the enemy fire their gravity wave cannon,

00:15:44.260 --> 00:15:46.160
all the missiles would detonate,

00:15:46.230 --> 00:15:48.960
and even our space-time contortion
buffer would be overwhelmed.

00:15:49.300 --> 00:15:50.670
Then where is the enemy?

00:15:50.870 --> 00:15:52.130
He'll be back!

00:15:52.670 --> 00:15:55.800
First strike scores the most!
Current heading, all ahead full!

00:15:56.140 --> 00:15:57.840
Enemy has not changed heading.

00:15:58.180 --> 00:16:00.580
Passing by the missile screen and accelerating.

00:16:01.050 --> 00:16:02.480
I guess we misjudged.

00:16:02.650 --> 00:16:04.550
What will we do, Captain?

00:16:04.650 --> 00:16:06.920
Since our plan of luring him into
the missile screen has failed,

00:16:06.920 --> 00:16:08.320
we should raise our...

00:16:08.320 --> 00:16:09.480
You don't have to be worried.

00:16:09.820 --> 00:16:11.910
Akito and the others will handle this just fine.

00:16:12.420 --> 00:16:14.420
Man, this had better work, damn it.

00:16:14.790 --> 00:16:18.130
I don't want to find myself all alone
when I charge at the enemy!

00:16:18.500 --> 00:16:21.600
Sprinkle your feed, watch
the fish swarm about.

00:16:21.600 --> 00:16:24.630
Dump in that hook with
the bait at the end.

00:16:24.840 --> 00:16:27.810
Spend the day with the line in the water...

00:16:27.810 --> 00:16:30.040
...and be rewarded with a huge catch!

00:16:36.680 --> 00:16:37.650
Alright!

00:16:37.880 --> 00:16:39.980
All Aestivalis, follow me!

00:16:40.950 --> 00:16:42.180
Here we go!

00:16:46.660 --> 00:16:48.790
This is Akatsuki-ki, come in, Nadesico!

00:16:49.030 --> 00:16:50.230
We landed the big one!

00:16:50.230 --> 00:16:52.410
Repeat, landed the big one!

00:16:51.060 --> 00:16:52.420
Charge!

00:16:55.700 --> 00:16:57.100
Bring the phase transition engine back online!

00:16:57.670 --> 00:16:59.470
Distortion field, maximum strength!

00:16:59.770 --> 00:17:02.300
Establish gravitron wave beam
link to all Aestivalis!

00:17:02.570 --> 00:17:03.740
Just leave it to me!

00:17:03.940 --> 00:17:04.640
Aye.

00:17:05.380 --> 00:17:07.240
Five enemy humanoid fighters
closing in rapidly!

00:17:07.480 --> 00:17:09.280
Approaching from directly
above and directly below!

00:17:09.350 --> 00:17:11.780
Bogey on scope! Enemy vessel dead ahead.
Heading directly at us!

00:17:11.920 --> 00:17:12.540
What?!

00:17:12.720 --> 00:17:13.410
He's good.

00:17:14.050 --> 00:17:19.920
The enemy's aim was to draw us into
range of their humanoid fighters.

00:17:20.530 --> 00:17:21.690
Ready all systems for intercept!

00:17:25.230 --> 00:17:28.430
For a person who didn't want
to fight against fellow humans,

00:17:28.430 --> 00:17:30.740
you certainly came up with a breathtaking tactic.

00:17:30.740 --> 00:17:33.730
I won't let the Nadesico lose a
battle until this war is over.

00:17:34.010 --> 00:17:34.900
And...

00:17:35.270 --> 00:17:37.760
This is the only place Akito has to come home to.

00:17:38.110 --> 00:17:42.100
Akito-kun again. What do you see
in a wimpy boy like him?

00:17:42.580 --> 00:17:44.640
Akito is always trying his best!

00:17:44.950 --> 00:17:47.650
Watching Akito push himself as
best as he can in everything...

00:17:47.650 --> 00:17:50.420
...makes me feel that I can try
harder in what I'm doing.

00:17:54.060 --> 00:17:55.550
All units, maintain maximum field strength.

00:17:55.690 --> 00:17:58.060
Our target is the point where the
boson emission is the strongest.

00:17:58.160 --> 00:17:58.720
Got it?!

00:17:58.900 --> 00:17:59.420
Roger!

00:18:07.940 --> 00:18:11.000
Enemy units have attached to
the space-time contortion field.

00:18:11.410 --> 00:18:13.900
Losing control of contortion field.
Collapse is imminent!

00:18:14.150 --> 00:18:14.800
Captain!

00:18:14.950 --> 00:18:15.840
Calm down!

00:18:16.310 --> 00:18:18.840
Let the arthropodal fighters
handle intercepting the enemy.

00:18:19.580 --> 00:18:20.780
Locked on to enemy vessel position!

00:18:21.190 --> 00:18:23.150
Aim leap gun at enemy vessel.

00:18:29.290 --> 00:18:31.230
Boson readings. So that's it!

00:18:34.000 --> 00:18:35.900
Hostile craft has breached the buffer!

00:18:35.970 --> 00:18:37.460
Keep it away from the leap cannon!

00:18:38.540 --> 00:18:39.260
Saburota!

00:18:39.870 --> 00:18:41.400
Let me borrow the Denjin!

00:18:46.540 --> 00:18:47.570
Got it!

00:18:48.250 --> 00:18:50.610
Wait a second! Increased boson readings!

00:18:50.920 --> 00:18:51.900
All units disperse!

00:18:52.020 --> 00:18:52.640
Roger!

00:18:54.020 --> 00:18:56.150
Come on! Now you have
the Denjin to deal with!

00:19:00.260 --> 00:19:01.990
Big ain't beautiful, you bastard!

00:19:02.160 --> 00:19:03.560
This time it's Riku Gangar?

00:19:03.860 --> 00:19:05.120
Clumsy Goliath...

00:19:05.830 --> 00:19:06.630
Whoa!

00:19:07.070 --> 00:19:10.300
Righteousness always prevails!

00:19:12.000 --> 00:19:13.330
Not that easily!

00:19:14.170 --> 00:19:16.660
That mecha design screams
that its rear is the weak point.

00:19:19.110 --> 00:19:20.670
Well, geez. Seriously?

00:19:20.810 --> 00:19:22.280
All units, fall back at maximum speed!

00:19:22.610 --> 00:19:25.670
Forgive me, Captain. Emergency leap!

00:19:26.550 --> 00:19:27.580
Saburota!

00:19:33.220 --> 00:19:36.490
That hot shot, he leaped to save the ship.

00:19:38.630 --> 00:19:40.630
Captain! It's the executive officer!

00:19:40.630 --> 00:19:41.260
What?!

00:19:41.730 --> 00:19:44.070
I am currently adrift inside the life pod.

00:19:44.570 --> 00:19:47.770
I would be most grateful if
you could retrieve me.

00:19:48.370 --> 00:19:49.940
Let's go get him.

00:19:49.940 --> 00:19:50.500
Aye!

00:19:51.210 --> 00:19:54.110
Our dear executive officer
certainly is a handful.

00:19:55.450 --> 00:19:58.610
The enemy vessel is withdrawing from the
combat area while laying down covering fire.

00:19:58.980 --> 00:20:02.250
We have not suffered any losses.
All Aestivalis units are well.

00:20:02.750 --> 00:20:05.690
Chart a course to Earth once we
have retrieved the Aestivalis wing.

00:20:05.860 --> 00:20:07.380
Keep an eye on the enemy, please.

00:20:14.800 --> 00:20:16.770
Captain, dispatch from the enemy vessel.

00:20:17.370 --> 00:20:20.570
I pay my respects to the bold and
courageous leadership of your vessel.

00:20:20.570 --> 00:20:23.170
I'm taken aback to learn a dashing
man of action such as yourself...

00:20:23.170 --> 00:20:25.170
...is in the dastardly United Earth Federation.

00:20:25.610 --> 00:20:28.710
We shall lock horns on the field
of battle again sometime.

00:20:28.710 --> 00:20:31.270
Captain of the Kannazuki, Genpachiro Akiyama.

00:20:31.420 --> 00:20:32.350
End quote.

00:20:32.620 --> 00:20:33.710
What?!

00:20:34.020 --> 00:20:35.540
What's this about a dashing man of action?!

00:20:35.950 --> 00:20:38.680
I'm a cute and adorable little girl!

00:20:42.230 --> 00:20:45.190
Preview

00:20:45.810 --> 00:20:48.410
Say, let me talk about my
older brother. This was...

00:20:47.060 --> 00:20:50.400
Around and around...

00:20:48.410 --> 00:20:50.350
I'm missing my underwear, my brassier.

00:20:50.350 --> 00:20:52.220
I think it was back when
I was in junior high school.

00:20:52.220 --> 00:20:54.890
My brother had an accident on his
way back from Mars to the Moon.

00:20:54.890 --> 00:20:57.290
My brother had an accident when he
was six, in front of the guests.

00:20:55.410 --> 00:21:02.250
Goes the fateful life of

00:20:57.290 --> 00:20:58.690
Hope you had diapers on hand.

00:20:58.860 --> 00:21:00.930
So, father suddenly started
expecting a whole lot out of me.

00:20:58.910 --> 00:21:02.250
a mahjong warrior

00:21:00.930 --> 00:21:02.990
It sure became uncomfortable fast.

00:21:03.060 --> 00:21:05.160
The next episode of
Martian Successor Nadesico:

00:21:03.210 --> 00:21:07.170
The flow of time

00:21:04.370 --> 00:21:07.170
begins to change

00:21:05.160 --> 00:21:06.870
"The 'Meadows' We Once Ran Across!"

00:21:07.100 --> 00:21:09.530
The U that comes before V and W! Preview.

00:21:08.250 --> 00:21:14.220
Next Episode

00:21:08.250 --> 00:21:14.220
The "Meadows" We Once Ran Across

00:21:09.530 --> 00:21:11.000
Do you mind?
